## Why This Is Asked

This tests practical transfer learning on small data, calibration awareness, and a simple data-collection loop.

## Key Concepts

- Transfer learning with lightweight nets
- Data augmentation for small datasets
- Probability calibration (temperature scaling)
- Active/incremental labeling
- Evaluation: accuracy and calibration metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: load pretrained MobileNetV2, replace head, train on 2k images
const model = loadPretrained('MobileNetV2');
model.detachHead();
model.addHead(5);
model.freezeLayers(['conv1','conv2']);
model.compile({lr: 1e-4, loss: 'categoricalCrossentropy', optimizer:'adam'});
model.fit(dataset, {epochs: 5, augment: true});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this with a simple active-learning loop?
- What failure modes could undermine calibration on unseen classes?

## Why This Is Asked
This checks practical CV setup, leakage awareness, and model selection on small data.

## Key Concepts
- Data leakage prevention
- Stratified cross-validation
- Pipeline preprocessing
- Model comparison metrics (AUROC, calibration)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: stratified K-fold CV in JS-like syntax
const k = 5;
const folds = stratifiedKFoldSplit(labels, k);
for (const [trainIdx, testIdx] of folds) {
  const model = trainLogisticRegression(features[trainIdx], labels[trainIdx]);
  const preds = model.predictProba(features[testIdx]);
  console.log(rocAuc(labels[testIdx], preds));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle class imbalance if AUROC is similar across models?
- How could you incorporate feature engineering without leaking future information?
